  "limitations": [
    "The rejection does not identify which loader format, size or authentication check failed.",
    "The dedicated recovery image has no kernel; fastboot boot sends it unchanged and does not automatically combine stock kernel or companion ramdisks.",
    "Fastboot lock state differs from Android properties; the positively parsed bootloader unlocked result was used for the authorized trial.",
    "The compiled static artifact milestone remains a historical record, not a claim that hardware testing succeeded.",
    "The v4 wrapper was accepted but reached stock Android. Public Qualcomm loader code suggests init_boot ramdisk preference; the proprietary Nezha loader implementation has not been established.",
    "No partition-write, wipe, unlock/relock, or slot-change command was sent. Temporary boot does not guarantee that a bootloader leaves all of its internal boot metadata unchanged.",
    "The v3 trial has saved first-stage initialization failure evidence. TWRP UI, recovery ADB and recovery logs remain unverified; saved previous-kernel logs are distinct from a working recovery logger.",
    "The directory-scaffold trial reached second-stage recovery init with SELinux enforcing. Init then rebooted; its fatal cause was not visible amid kernel write-rate-limit suppression. This is not a completed TWRP UI/ADB startup.",
    "Attempt 5 identifies the missing /apex mount point from a fresh saved kernel log. Its earlier stale DropBox capture is retained but excluded as evidence of that trial; BootReceiver can publish after sys.boot_completed.",
    "Attempt 6 adds the empty /apex directory, but an accepted boot command and absent USB do not prove TWRP started or the phone crashed. Screen state and the current runtime remain unresolved.",
    "The config-directory candidate was initially recorded before upload or boot; that preparation checkpoint remains historical. Static absence of /config is a USB setup defect, not proof that it is the only runtime problem in attempt 6.",
    "Attempt 7 was accepted but USB remained absent during the bounded observation. Adding /config alone did not establish working USB, UI or authenticated ADB; the actual startup failure still needs runtime evidence.",
    "After attempt 7 the user returned to fastboot, and one authorized diagnostic reboot returned the verified stock build on slot a. Early read-only DropBox collection observed a SYSTEM_BOOT entry but no SYSTEM_LAST_KMSG candidate within its 90-second monotonic budget. The observed forward phone-clock correction does not establish why the kernel log is missing or what recovery stage failed."
  ],
